invariant: INV-14
file: src/jws.c
catches: jws_test
reason: verify_eddsa answers CH_EAUTH for a key that is not 32 bytes.
  jws.h gives the two refusals to two owners: a key the call cannot take
  is the caller's to correct, CH_EINVAL, and a signature that does not
  verify is the token's fault, CH_EAUTH. A caller that logs CH_EINVAL as
  its own error and counts CH_EAUTH as a failed login then hides a wrong
  key in its login counters. bin/jws_test passes a P-256 key under EdDSA
  and requires CH_EINVAL.

--- old
    if (key_len != ED25519_KEY_LEN) {
        return CH_EINVAL;
    }
--- new
    if (key_len != ED25519_KEY_LEN) {
        return CH_EAUTH;
    }
